Developer pushes code to GitLab
        ↓
GitLab Runner picks up the job
        ↓
Pulls custom Python image (Python 3.12 + ODBC Driver 18 + pip packages)
  Image: registry.gitlab.com/mandtbank/mtb/cl7/test-automation/database-tests/sql-unit-test
        ↓
Spins up SQL Server 2022 as a sidecar service container
  Image: registry.gitlab.com/mandtbank/mtb/cl7/test-automation/database-tests/mssql2022
        ↓
python3.12 tests/setup_db.py
  │
  ├── Polls SQL Server until ready (up to 30 retries × 5s)
  ├── Creates TestDB database (IF NOT EXISTS)
  ├── Executes 01_create_tables.sql  → 5 tables
  └── Executes 02_create_procedures.sql → 2 stored procedures
        ↓
pytest tests/ --junitxml=test-results.xml --html=test-report.html
  │
  ├── sql_test_parser.py discovers all @@TEST blocks in testcases/*.sql
  ├── test_sql_runner.py parametrizes 13 test cases
  ├── clean_tables fixture truncates all tables before EACH test
  ├── For each test case:
  │     1. Run body SQL (INSERT setup data + EXEC stored procedure)
  │     2. Run each @@ASSERT query (must return 1=PASS, 0=FAIL)
  │     3. Collect failures → fail with combined message
  └── Results written to XML + HTML
        ↓
Artifacts saved to GitLab:
  ├── test-results.xml   ← visible in MR → Tests tab (pass/fail per test)
  └── test-report.html   ← downloadable HTML report (30-day retention)
        ↓
SQL Server sidecar container destroyed
